From: Djair Guilherme <djair.jr@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: do not emit fence.tso by default (T-Head C906)

The SG2002's T-Head C906 core does not implement fence.tso: it raises an
illegal-instruction exception instead of executing it as the plain fence
the encoding falls back to (fence.tso is FENCE with fm=1000, defined so
that cores without Ztso run it as fence rw,rw). GCC emits fence.tso for
__atomic_thread_fence(__ATOMIC_ACQ_REL), so C++ code (libstdc++ shared_ptr
release, 60 sites in libstdc++.so) died with SIGILL on the camera.

Make -mno-fence-tso the default: the compiler then emits fence rw,rw, a
strictly stronger barrier, so ordering is preserved. -mfence-tso turns it
back on for other cores. reCamera F7, docs/multimedia.md §6.2.

--- a/gcc/config/riscv/riscv.opt	2026-10-19 15:53:01.891273876 -0300
+++ b/gcc/config/riscv/riscv.opt	2026-10-19 15:53:01.893273829 -0300
@@ -675,7 +675,7 @@
 Specify TLS dialect.
 
 mfence-tso
-Target Var(TARGET_FENCE_TSO) Init(1)
+Target Var(TARGET_FENCE_TSO) Init(0)
 Specifies whether the fence.tso instruction should be used.
 
 mautovec-segment
